}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Brave Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Dark Cat''' when obtained from [[Hyperberserker (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the original Axe Cat, Brainwashed Axe Cat suffers from its extreme cost efficiency issue, making it just as useless against Traitless enemies as traited ones. The same applies for its [[Curse]] ability as Traitless enemies tend to be stat-based rather than ability-focused, greatly reducing the amount of relevant targets ([[Henry]], [[Croakley]], [[Mr. Mole]], etc.). Even if these enemies are put aside, others are either too weak (Doge, Snache, etc) or have enough brute force (R.Ost, etc) to nullify its niche. Needless to say, it is of no use other than collection. Even considering its potential as a meatshield, it's heavily outclassed by [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] and even a unit in its own set, [[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Tank Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
This unit doesn't change much in its True Form. It gains a health boost and guaranteed level 1 mini-wave. This does extend its attack range and curse ability, but overall contributes little, and as such it remains outclassed by vastly superior alternatives. A terrible True Form overall.

